# Shape only, never real values. Phase 0/1 (Scout + dashboard shell) need
# NO credentials at all — leaderboard, positions, activity, and market
# resolution data are all public, unauthenticated endpoints (verified
# live, see docs/PRD.md §9). This file exists for later phases:
#
# Phase 3 (Mandates / LLM) — via OpenRouter, not a direct Anthropic key.
# Both required together — scout logs mandate.disabled and skips mandate
# issuance entirely if either is missing, no crash. Put comments on their
# own line, never trailing a real value — docker-compose's env_file
# directive does NOT strip inline "# comments" the way a shell `source`
# would (see .env's own note, and sources/openrouter.py).
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=            # e.g. deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731 — the model this
                                # project's own code was actually verified live against
                                # (2026-08-08); any OpenRouter model slug works, but a
                                # different one may need mandate/issue.py's ISSUE_MAX_TOKENS
                                # and reasoning-effort tuned if it's also a reasoning model

# Phase 4 (on-chain event subscription):
# POLYGON_RPC_URL=

# Telegram (config-write surface):
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# Phase 6 (live trading only — CLOB order signing):
# POLYMARKET_PRIVATE_KEY=
